{"sourceSha256": "c3161d27b2532c5b8547abc18a6fc4d1f8bce9b578978e5eeebd4f0eed164c48", "text": "Dear Dr. McArdle,\n\nPatient: Mr Yanlin Ma\nD.0.B: 12/03/1986\n\n| am writing to refer this patient, a 32-year-old intemational student who needs follow up\n\ncare following open-chest surgery two weeks ago.\n\nHe presented to the hospital two weeks ago with signs and symptoms of acute pulmonary\noedema for which he underwent urgent cardiothoracic surgery for repair of dissection and\naortic root replacement with a mechanical valve due to associated aortic valve\nIncompetence. Despite being mildly hypertensive curing the first 3 days postoperatively, he\nhas made a satisfactory recovery and complied with a physiotherapy exercise program.\n\nAt discharge he is taking a range of medications including antibiotics, analgesics and blood\nthinning medication. He was prescribed Warfarin (3mg mocte) and his INR needs to be\nmaintained at between 2.5-3.5. His pain medication (Endone) should be stopped when\npossible and he can be weaned off isosorbide mononitrate and clonidine when his blood\npressure stabilises. He will be reviewed at the cardiac clinic in 3 months time.\n\nMr Ma has a 2-year history of hypertension and his father cied of aortic aneurism at 44 years\nof age. He is a smoker and ts overweight (BMI 30) for which education including smoking\ncessation and weight loss was provided as well as referral to Toowong Cardiac\n\nRehabilitation.\nDo not hesitate to contact me should you have any further quenes.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. Ross Mcintyre\n\nCardiothoracic Surgeon\nSpirit Hospital", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr. McArdle,\n\nPatient: Mr Yanlin Ma\nD.0.B: 12/03/1986\n\n| am writing to refer this patient, a 32-year-old intemational student who needs follow up\n\ncare following open-chest surgery two weeks ago.\n\nHe presented to the hospital two weeks ago with signs and symptoms of acute pulmonary\noedema for which he underwent urgent cardiothoracic surgery for repair of dissection and\naortic root replacement with a mechanical valve due to associated aortic valve\nIncompetence. Despite being mildly hypertensive curing the first 3 days postoperatively, he\nhas made a satisfactory recovery and complied with a physiotherapy exercise program.\n\nAt discharge he is taking a range of medications including antibiotics, analgesics and blood\nthinning medication. He was prescribed Warfarin (3mg mocte) and his INR needs to be\nmaintained at between 2.5-3.5. His pain medication (Endone) should be stopped when\npossible and he can be weaned off isosorbide mononitrate and clonidine when his blood\npressure stabilises. He will be reviewed at the cardiac clinic in 3 months time.\n\nMr Ma has a 2-year history of hypertension and his father cied of aortic aneurism at 44 years\nof age. He is a smoker and ts overweight (BMI 30) for which education including smoking\ncessation and weight loss was provided as well as referral to Toowong Cardiac\n\nRehabilitation.\nDo not hesitate to contact me should you have any further quenes.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDr. Ross Mcintyre\n\nCardiothoracic Surgeon\nSpirit Hospital", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2107.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr. McArdle,", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr. McArdle,", "x": 0.01139, "y": 0.00464, "width": 0.1832, "height": 0.02607, "confidence": 0.958, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.01139, "width": 0.04651, "confidence": 0.963}, {"text": "Dr.", "x": 0.06882, "width": 0.02943, "confidence": 0.95}, {"text": "McArdle,", "x": 0.10299, "width": 0.0916, "confidence": 0.96}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Patient: Mr Yanlin Ma\nD.0.B: 12/03/1986", "lines": [{"text": "Patient: Mr Yanlin Ma", "x": 0.01329, "y": 0.06321, "width": 0.22639, "height": 0.01286, "confidence": 0.923, "words": [{"text": "Patient:", "x": 0.01329, "width": 0.08068, "confidence": 0.96}, {"text": "Mr", "x": 0.10299, "width": 0.02943, "confidence": 0.886}, {"text": "Y